# Secure AI Gateway, project rules

Always read docs/PROJECT_BRIEF.md before making changes. It defines what
this project is and what each module is responsible for.

## Absolute rules
- Never use print(). All logging goes through the logger in
  src/core/logging_setup.py, which writes to stderr only. A single stray
  print breaks the MCP stdio transport in src/mcp_server.
- Never hardcode API keys, tokens or secrets. Read them from
  src/core/config.py, which loads from .env.
- Never commit .env or anything in data/.

## Style
- Python 3.11+, type hints on every function signature.
- Validate all external input with Pydantic v2 models using
  model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid").
- Async throughout the FastAPI services. Use httpx.AsyncClient for all
  outbound HTTP. Do not use the openai or groq SDKs.
- Keep logic out of route handlers. Routes parse input and delegate.

## Structure
- Shared code lives in src/core and is imported, never copied.
- src/mcp_server is Task 1. src/mcp_gateway is Task 2.
  src/llm_gateway is Tasks 3 and 4.
- Test doubles live only in tests/fault_injection and are never imported
  by anything under src/.

## Errors
- Outward facing errors are short and contain no stack traces, provider
  names, file paths or internal details.
- Full detail goes to the log and the audit table under a matching error id.

## Testing
- Every module gets a matching test file in tests/.
- Never weaken a test to make it pass.
